# Static Fields at the Top of the File

All `static` fields (constants, caches, counters) belong at the **top of the class**, immediately after the class declaration and together with other static members — **not** between instance fields and methods in the middle of the file.

## Order (typical)

1. `public static final` / `private static final` constants
2. Other `static` fields (if any)
3. Instance fields
4. Constructors, methods, nested types (if allowed)

## Do not do this

```java
public class Buildable {
    private Template template;

    public void build() { ... }

    private static final int INSTANT_BUILD_EXTERIOR_MARGIN_BLOCKS = 4; // ❌ mid-file

    protected void instantFinishBuildTask() { ... }
}
```

## Do this

```java
public class Buildable {
    private static final int INSTANT_BUILD_EXTERIOR_MARGIN_BLOCKS = 4;

    private Template template;

    public void build() { ... }

    protected void instantFinishBuildTask() { ... }
}
```

## Agent behavior

When adding or moving a `static` field, place it with the existing static block at the top. If you touch a file that has a static constant buried mid-class, move it to the top in the same change.
